  - Born rule
  - differential privacy
  - GDPR
  - information-theoretic security
  - one-time pad
abstract: >
  We present the first data anonymization system whose irreversibility is guaranteed
  by the Born rule of quantum mechanics rather than by computational hardness
  assumptions. We introduce QRNG-OTP-Destroy, a protocol that replaces each
  personally identifiable value with a quantum-random token and irreversibly destroys
  the mapping. We formalize three tiers of irreversibility (computational,
  information-theoretic, physics-guaranteed), prove that no classical PRNG-based
  method achieves the strongest tier, and prove that QRNG-OTP-Destroy does.
